WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.280
My name is Juzo Inui.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.150
After the great war, the city
overflowed with Extendeds,

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.980
people who underwent
physical function extensions...

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.610
What? You're sick of hearing this?

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.980
Now don't be like that.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.610
The job this time is a little
different from my regular jobs.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:38.650
I mean, it's the job that triggered
me to follow this line of work.

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.780
Will you protect my sister?

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.360
Victor is in the Kyusei Pit...

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:23.980
Client

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.230
Juzo.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:24.820
You met Victor for the first
time during the war, right?

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:29.570
He was my personal engineer for a while.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.650
He was a good guy.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.280
Even to us Extendeds, who most
people keep their distance with.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.440
I can't believe he's still alive...

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.320
Victor...

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.190
The Victor I knew was kind...

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.610
He always tried to help others.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.230
That's why...

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.320
Yeah.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.530
I can't believe it myself.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.360
Victor, being a part of a
terrorist organization...

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.320
That's not it.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:08.440
It's true that the Victor I knew
would never hurt anyone.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.650
But...

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.860
Did I ever tell you that we were orphans?

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.320
We were both taken in by
an engineer named Emmet.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:25.480
It seems he wanted someone as a successor.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:31.650
Victor was good with his hands,
so he was given jobs pretty quickly.

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:35.730
That was probably when
Victor first got interested

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:40.570
in the newly emerging
extension technology at the time.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:46.650
Things started going wrong
between the two of them...

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.980
Our old man started getting angry often.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:52.480
Victor started taking care
of the shop all by himself.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:16.190
He probably held an aversion
to extension technology.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:21.860
Sometime after that,
Victor disappeared from my life.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.320
He left me all alone.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:33.360
Are you telling me that
Victor killed that old man?

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:38.820
After that, I got a single letter telling me
he became an army engineer in the war.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.320
That's it.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.780
To begin with...

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.280
...maybe I never really understood
anything about Victor.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.650
That's why I'm going to confirm
things with my own eyes.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:51.650
Anyways!

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.150
This is a personal family problem!

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:57.860
There's no need for you to get involved, Juzo.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:58.730
Mary!

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.650
What? You can't get mad at me for this!

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.440
You need to focus on saving Chris and the boy--

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.570
Even if you didn't stick
your nose in our business,

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:18.230
we were destined to become enemies.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:24.320
You will regret the fact that you did
the extension procedures, Juzo Inui!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:33.320
Now... hand over the data.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:36.780
Juzo!

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.280
Stay back.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.980
Be careful.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:44.190
If I push this button, my comrades
will kill the hostages--

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.900
That's it?

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.900
You, who goes against
the providence of God.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:11.480
This anti-Extended full body armor has
compressed diamond nanofilaments

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:16.400
that are used in your artificial
muscles woven inside of it.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.360
Three times more than the amount
in a normal combat Extended!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:26.400
You cannot compete with this
power output and resilience!

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.690
Sh-Shimazu!

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.230
I'm thankful.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:45.400
I didn't have to pull my punches,
even though you don't have extensions.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:50.190
I was having trouble with my own
weak-mindedness about it.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.360
You monster.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.400
Where are the hostages?

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:55.900
Where'd you hide them?!

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:58.110
You seem pretty desperate.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:02.440
Well, terrorists without common
sense took my friends hostage.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.730
You thought you could negotiate with us?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.110
You fool.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.480
Existing as an Extended is a sin in itself!

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:17.440
The anger of those trampled by all of
you will be sure to destroy you all!

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.360
Just kill me. Your threats won't work.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.940
I wasn't planning on negotiating from the start.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:28.150
I sure hope you treat those hostages
well if you want the data.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.900
Otherwise, all of you bastards...

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.730
...will regret the fact that you ever
laid hands on my family in hell!

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.610
Let's go, Mary.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:44.190
Go? Go where, Juzo?

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.730
The Kyusei Pit.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.320
You're gonna look for Victor, right?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.150
Then we're heading in the same direction.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:55.980
I also got something I need to confirm with him.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:01.030
After all, it was the first job I ever accepted.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:02.940
Huh?

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:07.150
Victor asked me to protect you.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:11.230
That was the first job I ever accepted.

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:15.110
Protect me?

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:18.280
I was never told anything
about something like that?!

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:20.230
There wasn't a need to tell you.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:23.900
What?! Hold on, what do you mean?!

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.820
Please protect my sister, Mary!

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:38.230
But my client is going around with his
little friends and putting you in danger.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:42.480
That's a breach of contract.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:46.150
I have no idea what the hell happened,

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.070
but depending on the situation...

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:51.610
...I might have to beat the shit
out of him to set him straight.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:59.650
The Extended Resolver who took
Master Tetsuro under his wing...

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.230
Juzo Inui, was it?

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:09.980
It seems that man has defeated our attack unit.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:14.570
They were people who specialized only in battle.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:19.610
It seems they could not beat a monster
who surpassed the realm of man.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:23.860
Why is your hatred for the Extended so deep?

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:27.730
Not all Extended are evil.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:31.980
I find it strange to hear something
like that from you, Master Tetsuro.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.940
Please come this way.

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:43.320
Master Tetsuro.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:50.230
I am honored to welcome you back to Spitzbergen.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:57.980
As the organization's representative,
I thank you for your assistance, Master Tetsuro.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:00.110
Who are you?

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:03.780
It seems you have truly lost your memory.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:09.610
My name is Wachowski.

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:11.780
That name...

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:14.230
I was quite worried.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:22.190
I had heard you were sent to the Berühren
facility for funding our cause.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:26.030
However, you've come back to us.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:31.480
You even brought Harmony with you,
which has the power to shake this world.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.030
Funding?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:37.860
I was helping the terrorists of Spitzbergen?!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.900
That is correct.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.230
Impossible!

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.230
No.

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:44.690
You are a criminal who betrayed
your father's organization

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:47.730
and aided terrorists in their endeavors.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:56.230
That is the objective truth, Master Tetsuro.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.070
You said your name was Victor?

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.480
Yeah.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:22.070
Do you really understand
that I'm a Gun Slave Unit?

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.780
Of course I do.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.900
I'm your personal engineer.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.940
What in the world are you saying?

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:34.570
More importantly, we can't converse
while I'm doing your maintenance.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:38.150
In your case, I can't see
your facial expressions,

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:41.280
so if the pain gets unbearable...

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:42.730
Let's see.

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:49.400
Um... Gun... Gun head... I see... Then!

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.440
Give me a signal like this.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.650
It'll mean, "Help me!"

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.320
Juzo!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.690
Are you all right, Juzo?!

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.730
Making a face like that!

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.360
Mary. That's...

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:15.980
That's?

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.030
No.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:24.730
It just surprised me that people who
hate extensions, like Spitzbergen,

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:29.400
would be hiding in a nest of
Extendeds like the Kyusei Pit.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:33.650
Doesn't that make it the perfect hiding place?

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:38.980
And this place is a lawless zone.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:44.820
Even so, I'm surprised that the
Kyusei Group even let you in again.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:51.480
I'm sure they don't like the fact that
a terrorist group is living on their turf.

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:55.030
By the way, just now...

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:57.690
You said, "Making a face like that."

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:01.030
You make it sound like I have
expressions or something.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.230
What are you talking about?

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:07.570
Of course you do.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:09.860
You didn't know?

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:15.030
Oh.

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:17.190
Hey, I thought you'd come.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.280
Lefty! Where were you?!

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:23.150
Why are you sticking around us?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.820
Who the hell is controlling you?!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:32.780
Juzo. Lefty doesn't have a voice box,
so he won't be able to respond...

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:33.980
Huh?

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:40.610
Bastard, how did you...?

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:41.400
Huh?

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.730
Juzo, does this mean something?

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.610
Lefty! Wait!

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:56.480
It might be leading us to Victor again.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.860
Fine by me.

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:09.070
Mary, wait here.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.650
But Victor should be up ahead!

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:14.530
Victor might not be alone.

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:16.570
Even if you want to settle things with him,

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:21.030
there's no need for you to put
yourself recklessly in danger.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:25.820
And let me say this before
anything happens, Mary.

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:30.530
You understand what I mean by
"taking care of things" with him, right?

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:36.190
I might kill your big brother today.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:38.780
That depends on what happens.

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:41.900
Prepare yourself for that possibility.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.570
Got it...

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.440
Good girl.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.480
Jeez...

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:44.780
Empty Extended bodies.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:47.480
What terrible taste.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.530
Too bad.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.610
The hostages are being held in a different area.

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:57.070
This place is being watched
by the Reconstruction Agency.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:00.780
Expected as much.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:05.230
You haven't changed at all, Device 13.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.650
No, your name is different now.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:11.780
Now, it's Juzo.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:16.650
Seems you've changed a lot, Victor.

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:21.280
I heard people call you the Dismantler nowadays.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:24.650
Why are you siding with terrorists?

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:25.860
And what the hell are you doing,

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:31.570
putting your little sister in danger
after asking me to protect her?

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:37.030
It's been a long time since <i>then</i> ,
but you are still the same.

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:41.610
That foolish honesty. I really admire it.

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:49.030
I am lending them a hand in order
to reap what I've sown... So to say.

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:55.070
I never planned on involving Mary.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:58.730
Then, this hand Extended.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:02.780
Were you the one controlling this guy?

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.150
The reason you called me with it.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:09.070
Isn't it because you need me
to save you from something?

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.190
You're right.

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:18.820
The me <i>back then</i> hasn't changed
at all since that <i>request</i> , Juzo.

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:22.190
So...

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.440
How should I put this...?

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:34.940
This looks just like what I imagine
a den for terrorists would look.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:38.440
I believe it wouldn't have hurt
to be a little more creative?

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.820
You're the bastard from the
Reconstruction Agency.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.070
You tailed me here.

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:45.360
I finally get to meet you.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:53.610
I'm sure you had no idea about it,
but I've always dreamed of this moment.

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:56.900
Victor the Dismantler!

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:02.400
This moment, where I capture you
after chasing you all these years!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:04.530
Victor Steinberg.

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:10.610
You are under arrest for 32 charges of
murder and attempted murder!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:22.570
I feel bad since you came all the way here,

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:27.070
but this guy is my client
before being a terrorist.

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:30.400
Mr. Inui, I do not understand.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:33.230
Your friends were kidnapped by them.

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:35.480
That means you are a victim.

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:36.480
So, why?

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.690
Yeah.

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:43.780
I don't really get it myself.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:46.030
I see. Fine.

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:51.150
You are also on our watch list
of dangerous people.

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.480
Juzo Inui.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:56.730
For the crimes of aiding terrorists
and obstructing the line of duty...

00:18:56.730 --> 00:19:01.610
As the substitute director of EMS,
you are under arrest.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:05.190
Sistivas Skopendra.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.940
You protected me?!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:22.530
N-No way...!

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:30.480
Juzo!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.940
Mary! Stay back!

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:34.980
I was waiting for you.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.780
Stop!

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:40.820
Mary!

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:43.190
Victor, you bastard!
What the hell are you doing?!

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:47.530
Perfect. Now, everything has been prepared.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:54.820
Looks like you're no longer
the Victor I know.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.610
That's not true.

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:59.150
I haven't changed at all.

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:01.150
I wanted to know.

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:03.400
Ever since then...

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:10.230
...just what is inside those extensions that
surpass humans in bodily functions?

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:15.780
That's why I want to examine an
exquisite extension like your body.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:19.030
I want to dismantle you so bad!

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:24.190
If you want to take me apart, feel free.

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:26.650
There's no need to involve Mary.

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:29.820
That's no good. It's not.

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:33.070
You don't have a Hands.

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:41.230
That means that I can only see your true
form when you put your life on the line!

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:47.730
My true form?

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:52.820
That's right, you really haven't
changed at all since then.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:55.440
Just like how you protected me earlier.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.150
You can only use your power
if it's to help someone else.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:05.150
In order to protect the ones you love,
you would even sacrifice your own self.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:11.480
In other words, my request to protect Mary.

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:14.860
It's time for you to finish that job to the end.

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:18.860
You understand me, right?

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:24.280
I wasn't protecting you.

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:35.780
I was protecting her dream of meeting her
good-for-nothing brother that left her.

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:39.570
Protecting Mary's feelings!

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:45.650
And, it goes without saying...

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:50.480
I'm going to beat your ass right now.

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:52.150
Your request!

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:55.900
I'll make sure to fulfill it!

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:29.190
Quit joking around.

00:23:28.230 --> 00:23:30.150
If I could meet you again,
I wanted to say one thing...

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:31.570
Did you forget? My other name...

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:32.860
If I could meet you again,
I wanted to say one thing...

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:31.570
You coward!

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:35.440
Victor!

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:35.440
I'll strip it down!

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:41.530
<i>NO GUNS LIFE</i> . Episode 15.
"A Place to Call Home."
